{:edb/db-before-t 2186 :edb/db-after-t 2187 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535499 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:18:09.229Z" 13194139535499 true] [17592186078306 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352293 13194139535499 true] [17592186078306 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352307 13194139535499 true] [17592186078307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352300 13194139535499 true] [17592186078307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352303 13194139535499 true] [17592186260013 1145 "We know that the surface area of a cube with side length $s$ is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(s)=6{s}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(s)$ with respect to $s$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{'}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(6{s}^{2}) \\\\  & =6(2s) \\\\  & =12s,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=3$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{'}(3)=12(3)=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the cube is changing when its side length is $3\\,\\text{in}$, is $36$ ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" 13194139535499 false] [17592186260013 1145 "We know that the surface area of a cube with side length $s$ is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(s)=6{s}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(s)$ with respect to $s$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(6{s}^{2}) \\\\  & =6(2s) \\\\  & =12s,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=3$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(3)=12(3)=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the cube is changing when its side length is $3\\,\\text{in}$, is $36$ ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352293 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352294 13194139535499 true] [17592186352293 1089 "q-170656" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352293 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535499 true] [17592186352293 1100 "The bases of a trapezoid are increasing and the larger base is always twice the smaller base. The height of the trapezoid is $2\\,cm.$ Find the rate of change of the area of the trapezoid with respect to its smaller base $b.$" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352293 1113 #uuid "334676cf-0dd1-5735-bc6e-72eb49b9359e" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352293 1145 "The area of a trapezoid is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(B+b)h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the smaller base, $B$ is the larger base and $h$ is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nWe are given that $B=2b$ and $h=2,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $B=2b$ and $h=2$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(b+2b)(2)}{2}=3b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$ with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(3b) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(b) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352295 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352296 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352297 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352298 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352299 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1041 "selection" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352296 13194139535499 true] [17592186352294 1110 #uuid "0d012542-7176-595f-bd94-312364df2fb2" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352295 1034 "4{b}^{2}" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352295 1111 #uuid "4e83a5ba-83b1-5620-9b77-a5f9ceca89a3" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352296 1034 "3" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352296 1111 #uuid "6f252992-bbb8-5043-9dda-2fb3232020cc" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352297 1034 "3b" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352297 1111 #uuid "160e7109-21ba-583a-bf44-dddea22b35d1" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352298 1034 "b" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352298 1111 #uuid "3cbe346f-7894-54d3-afe6-23233fd890e5" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352299 1034 "{b}^{2}" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352299 1111 #uuid "31500ce3-c0a2-5695-87c2-0cbd39a07e50" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352300 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352301 13194139535499 true] [17592186352300 1089 "q-343169" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352300 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535499 true] [17592186352300 1100 "Air is pumped into and released from a pressurized chamber. After $t$ minutes, the volume of air (in cubic meters) is modeled by\n\n$$\nA(t)=-6{t}^{2}+90t+400,\\,0\\le t\\le 15.\n$$\n\nFind the exact value of the instantaneous rate of change of the air volume with respect to time when $t=7$ minutes.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change when $t=7$ minutes is\n{{field-1}} cubic meters per minute." 13194139535499 true] [17592186352300 1113 #uuid "750bc4e7-798f-5eba-ad9f-61537ac1f813" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352300 1145 "The instantaneous rate of change of the air volume at $t=7$ minutes is ${A}^{′}(7).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}\\,(-6{t}^{2}+90t+400) \\\\  & =-12t+90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(7) & =-12(7)+90 \\\\  & =-84+90 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the air volume at $t=7$ minutes is $6$ cubic meters per minute." 13194139535499 true] [17592186352301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352302 13194139535499 true] [17592186352301 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535499 true] [17592186352301 1041 "field-1" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352301 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352302 13194139535499 true] [17592186352301 1110 #uuid "9a0248ff-1b8b-5b69-9237-e6c5c4d2985f" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352302 1034 "6" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352302 1111 #uuid "1977d7ab-32a5-5fc2-9e99-bb39ba2991b6" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352303 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352304 13194139535499 true] [17592186352303 1089 "q-343404" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352303 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535499 true] [17592186352303 1100 "The depth $D,$ in meters, of a plant’s root system after $t$ months is modeled by $D(t)=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2t+13}.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the root depth when $t=6$ months?\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change when $t=6$ months is\n{{field-1}} meters per month." 13194139535499 true] [17592186352303 1113 #uuid "42884ae8-06df-563a-81bb-8d8c47e48c56" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352303 1145 "The instantaneous rate of change of the root depth when $t=6$ months is equal to ${D}^{′}(6).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2t+13}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2t+13)^{(1/2)-1}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2t+13)^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{′}(6) & =\\frac{1}{4}(2(6)+13)^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the root depth when $t=6$ months is $\\frac{1}{20}$ meters per month." 13194139535499 true] [17592186352304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352305 13194139535499 true] [17592186352304 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352306 13194139535499 true] [17592186352304 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535499 true] [17592186352304 1041 "field-1" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352304 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352306 13194139535499 true] [17592186352304 1110 #uuid "5b5419fb-8feb-57fd-b6a6-8e84ce71fbab" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352305 1034 "\\frac{1}{10}" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352305 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352305 1111 #uuid "4b4fd285-19ee-5346-a08a-1a8483262811" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352306 1034 "\\frac{1}{20}" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352306 1111 #uuid "08961285-718b-541f-a56a-3caea667241f" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352307 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352308 13194139535499 true] [17592186352307 1089 "q-48719" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352307 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535499 true] [17592186352307 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066378/assets/2b5d589462bf2477be3d305ea88f3d5462b7d6ea4e001a9a71790d53e1683665.png)\n\nThe area of the square above is increasing. The length of the side of the square is $l.$ Find the rate of change of the area of a square with respect to the length of its side." 13194139535499 true] [17592186352307 1113 #uuid "062fcd02-d338-5b14-8c30-fb2aac436416" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352307 1145 "The area of the square is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(l)={l}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length of the side of the square.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(l)$ with respect to $l$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(l) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}l}({l}^{2})=2l.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352309 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352310 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352311 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352312 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352313 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1041 "selection" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352309 13194139535499 true] [17592186352308 1110 #uuid "4d013116-27c0-5024-a993-b98b4219b78b" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352309 1034 "2l" 13194139535499 true] [17592186352309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535499 true] [17592186352309 1111 #uuid "8f768e2d-a1e8-56c7-a93c-03